<%#
  Three rules inside 700px of scroll gave the nav, the byline and the related
  list the same weight as the end of the article itself, and each block then
  brought its own margin, so the gaps ran 32/48/28 with no rhythm to read. The
  page's own principle — a quiet label above the work, sections separated by
  space rather than lines — was already true everywhere except here. One rule
  closes the prose; below it a single `Stack` owns every gap, at the same
  `xxxl` the homepage puts between its sections.
%>

<footer class="pt-8 border-t border-mauve-6">
  <%= render Stack.new(space: :xxxl) do %>
    <div>
      <%= render PostFooterNav.new(
        previous_resource: @previous_resource,
        next_resource: @next_resource,
      ) %>

      <%#
        The share action belongs to the pair above it, not to the byline
        below, so it sits a `md` away from them and an `xxxl` from anything
        else. The margin rides on the button because the button ships hidden —
        a wrapper would hold the space open on every browser without the Web
        Share API.
      %>
      <%= render ShareButton.new(resource: @resource, class_name: "mt-4") %>
    </div>

    <%= render PostAuthor.new %>

    <%= render RelatedPosts.new(posts: helpers.related_posts(@resource)) %>
  <% end %>
</footer>
